From 459abae601411d191a1f4c99fe55b60d59e59305 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] server: accept external AudioChunk streams through avatar authority

Keep CyberVerse as the sole avatar/lip-sync/AV pacing/LiveKit publisher while
allowing an already-synthesized AudioChunk stream to enter the same internal
inference/media primitives used by the standard pipeline. The new HTTP ingress
is session scoped, sequence checked, fail-closed, and torn down with the
CyberVerse session. Yance does not gain WebRTC, JWT-signing, avatar, lip-sync,
resampling, or AV-pacing authority.
